htl.html`<pre class="lite-src">${ss.JSX_DECLS.trim()}</pre>`
// %%
md`## Appendix: this notebook's code

\`ss\` is imported from \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript\`. It is the object \`soundscript\` of \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-checker\`, assembled from ordinary cells: the checker and the per-cell compiler in that module, and the library that live cells call (state, actions, events, the JSX renderer) in \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime\`. The build generates both modules from the TypeScript sources. Only the parser, a third-party library, is a gzipped attachment. The example sources are attachments of this module, and the boxes and \`test_examples_check_as_expected\` read them; the live cells were compiled from the same files when the notebook was built.

Before each group of lesson cells is a \`sourceListing\` cell of this module. It shows the group's source, decompiled from the cells' live definitions and read again when the module's code changes, coloured with the editor's TypeScript parser (the core's \`ss_highlight\`). The lesson cells after it are shown as any cell is: a value with the normal Inspector, an action, a function, a listener, an events cell or a type as one line drawn by the core's \`ss_language.inspect\`, an element mounted, and a cell that does not check as its error.`
